WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.857
Two thousand years ago,

00:00:01.857 --> 00:00:05.314
an emperor asked the
question we still can't

00:00:05.314 --> 00:00:07.986
answer — not how to cure
sickness,

00:00:07.986 --> 00:00:09.950
but how to never need to.

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:14.309
Her answer was a calendar
that has never once lied.

00:00:14.309 --> 00:00:16.416
Four seasons. Four
instructions.

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:19.050
And a body that quietly
keeps the score.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:23.629
In spring, rise early and
give freely,

00:00:23.629 --> 00:00:25.355
or you wound the liver. In
summer,

00:00:25.355 --> 00:00:26.472
let your spirit bloom,

00:00:26.472 --> 00:00:28.300
and guard your temper like
treasure.

00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:33.400
Autumn, gather yourself
inward,

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.850
keep the lungs clear.
Winter,

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:35.950
seal your warmth away,

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:38.150
or spring finds your legs
too weak to stand.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:42.504
No season punishes itself.

00:00:42.504 --> 00:00:45.462
Each debt comes due in
the next.

00:00:45.462 --> 00:00:49.900
The same law that breaks
a body can dim the sun.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:53.518
The wise treat the illness
that hasn't arrived.

00:00:53.518 --> 00:00:56.200
Don't wait for thirst to dig
the well.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.035
The Emperor's Inner
Canon:

00:00:58.035 --> 00:00:59.800
The Four Seasons of Life.
